@startuml
skinparam monochrome true
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false

autonumber

actor "Editor" as Editor
participant ":System" as System

activate Editor


Editor -> System : asks to create a scenario for a selected map
activate System
System --> Editor : requests scenario period (start and end date)
deactivate System


Editor -> System : provides start and end date
activate System
System --> Editor : requests available locomotion types (diesel, electric, steam)
deactivate System
Editor -> System : indicates locomotion types to include in the scenario
activate System

loop for each locomotion type selected
    System --> Editor : requests availability date or indicate "always available" or "never available" for locomotion type
    deactivate System
    Editor -> System : provides availability date or indicates "always available" or "never available"
    activate System

    alt locomotion type becomes obsolete during scenario period
        System --> Editor : requests obsolescence date for locomotion type
        deactivate System
        Editor -> System : provides obsolescence date
        activate System
    end
end loop
        System --> Editor : requests cargo types to be part of the scenario
        deactivate System


Editor -> System : defines cargo types to be part of the scenario (Iron, Coal, Silver, etc.)
activate System
System --> Editor : requests cargo behavior (import, export, transform)
deactivate System

loop for each cargo type in scenario
    Editor -> System : defines behavior for cargo (import, export, transform)
    activate System
end loop
    System --> Editor : requests production frequency for generating industries
    deactivate System



Editor -> System : defines production frequency for generating industries (as a percentage)
activate System
System --> Editor : shows all data and asks for confirmation
deactivate System

' Editor confirma dados
Editor -> System : confirms data
activate System
System --> Editor : displays operation success
deactivate System
deactivate Editor

@enduml
